    "qualifierLines": [
      "{**23 NY3d at 18} OPINION OF THE COURT",
      " I concur in the majority's holding that the trial court erred in failing to issue the accomplice-in-fact instruction, because there was a reasonable view of the evidence that Mogavero \"participated in an offense based upon some of the same facts or conduct which ma[d]e up the offense on trial\" (People v Berger, 52 NY2d 214, 219 [1981]). In my view, however, that error was harmless because there was sufficient corroborating evidence tending to connect defendant to the commission{**23 NY3d at 30} of the crime and overwhelming evidence of his guilt. "
